    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1956-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "For \\(x\\ne\\pm2,\\) multiplying by \\(x^2-4\\) gives \\[ 15-2(x+2)=x^2-4. \\] Hence \\(x^2+2x-15=0,\\) so \\[ (x+5)(x-3)=0. \\] Both \\(x=-5\\) and \\(x=3\\) satisfy the domain restriction.\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "The original equation requires \\(x\\ne\\pm2\\)",
        "Multiply through by \\((x-2)(x+2)\\) and collect terms"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
